  "answer_text": "I cannot directly purchase tickets or handle payment transactions for you. However, I can walk you through the process, provide the schedules and options, and give you the direct links to book your return ticket.\n\nSince today is **Sunday, June 7, 2026**, \"next Friday\" could refer to either:\n*   **This coming Friday:** June 12, 2026\n*   **The following Friday:** June 19, 2026\n\nHere is how you can easily book your return ticket online:\n\n### Step 1: Go to the Booking Platform\nThe primary train operator between Boston and New York is **Amtrak**. \n*   **Book directly:** Go to the [Amtrak Official Website](https://www.amtrak.com).\n*   **Compare options:** If you want to compare prices across other dates or booking platforms, you can also use third-party tools like [Wanderu](https://www.wanderu.com) or [Omio](https://www.omio.com).\n\n### Step 2: Enter Your Travel Details\nWhen searching on the booking page, select **Round Trip** and input the following details:\n1.  **From (Origin):** `Boston, MA - South Station (BOS)` *(Alternatively, you can choose `Back Bay (BBY)` or `Route 128 (RTE)` if those stations are closer to you)*.\n2.  **To (Destination):** `New York, NY - Moynihan Train Hall at Penn Station (NYP)`.\n3.  **Depart Date:** Select Friday, June 12, 2026 (or June 19, 2026).\n4.  **Return Date:** Input the date you would like to travel back to Boston.\n\n### Step 3: Choose Your Train Type\nYou will be shown two main types of Amtrak trains for this route:\n*   **Northeast Regional:** This is the standard, budget-friendly option. It takes about **4 hours and 15 minutes**. Standard tickets typically range from $30 to $140 one-way depending on how early you book.\n*   **Acela:** This is Amtrak\u2019s high-speed service. It takes about **3 hours and 40 minutes** and offers business/first-class seating only. Tickets are generally more expensive.\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Tips for Saving Money:\n*   **Book ASAP:** Last-minute tickets on the Northeast Corridor can get expensive (sometimes over $200 one-way if booked on the day of travel). Booking right now for next Friday will secure a much lower fare.\n*   **Night Owl Fares:** If you don't mind traveling late at night or very early in the morning (between 6:00 PM and 8:00 AM), Amtrak offers special \"Night Owl\" fares between Boston and New York for as low as $20 one-way.",
